    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015-sch-1-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 After subsection 115.1(1) of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015#sch-1-sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was\nengaged in before 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on\nconviction by:\n\n(a) if, at the time the conduct was engaged in, the offence\nmentioned in paragraph (1)(e) was punishable on conviction\nby a term of imprisonment (other than imprisonment for\nlife)—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for a term of not\nmore than that term; or\n\n(b) otherwise—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.\n\n(1B) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was\nengaged in on or after 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on\nconviction by a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00163\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Harming Australians) Act 2015\nNo. 163, 2015",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was\nengaged in before 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on\nconviction by:\n\n(a) if, at the time the conduct was engaged in, the offence\nmentioned in paragraph (1)(e) was punishable on conviction\nby a term of imprisonment (other than imprisonment for\nlife)—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for a term of not\nmore than that term; or\n\n(b) otherwise—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.\n\n(1B) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was\nengaged in on or after 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on\nconviction by a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00163\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Harming Australians) Act 2015\nNo. 163, 2015",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015-sch-1-sec-5-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015-sch-1-sec-5-ss-1b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-harming-australians-act-2015#sch-1-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 After subsection 115.1(1) of the Criminal Code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was\nengaged in before 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on\nconviction by:\n\n(a) if, at the time the conduct was engaged in, the offence\nmentioned in paragraph (1)(e) was punishable on conviction\nby a term of imprisonment (other than imprisonment for\nlife)—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for a term of not\nmore than that term; or\n\n(b) otherwise—a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.\n\n(1B) If the conduct constituting an offence against subsection (1) was\nengaged in on or after 1 October 2002, the offence is punishable on\nconviction by a maximum penalty of imprisonment for life.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00163\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Harming Australians) Act 2015\nNo. 163, 2015"
    },
